---
title: Vegetarian Lettuce Wraps
---

In a #small bowl{}, stir together the @hoisin sauce{3%tbsp}, @soy sauce{3%tbsp}, @rice vinegar{2%tbsp}, and @sesame oil{1%tsp}. Set aside.

Press the @extra-firm tofu{1%package} (12- to 14-oz, do not use silken) between #paper towels{} to squeeze out as much liquid as possible. Refresh the paper towels and press again.

Heat the @canola oil{2%tsp} (or grapeseed oil) in a #large nonstick skillet{} over medium-high heat.

Once the oil is hot, crumble in the tofu, breaking it into very small pieces as it cooks.

Continue cooking for ~{5%minutes}, then add the finely chopped @baby bella cremini mushrooms{8%oz}.

Continue cooking until any remaining tofu liquid cooks off and the tofu starts to turn golden, about ~{3%minutes} more.

Stir in the drained and finely chopped @water chestnuts{1%can} (8 oz), minced @garlic{2%cloves}, freshly grated @ginger{2%tsp}, @red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp} (omit if sensitive to spice), and half of the thinly sliced @green onions{4}. Cook until fragrant, about ~{30%seconds} more.

Pour the sauce over the top of the tofu mixture and stir to coat. Cook just until you hear bubbling and the sauce is warmed through, ~{30-60%seconds}.

Spoon the tofu mixture into individual @romaine lettuce leaves{8%large} (from a romaine heart, or butter lettuce leaves). Top with the remaining green onions, grated @carrots{} (optional), and additional @red pepper flakes{} (optional) as desired. Enjoy immediately.
